  "dna": {
   "overview": "Black Dog is two organisms. The first is a phrase in A: an opening figure (E, G–G#–A, E, bent C), an answer with a triplet run on the G string, and a slide down the A string that lands on the open A. The second is John Paul Jones' 4½-beat cell: seven notes over nine eighths, played three times in 4/4, so every pass starts half a beat later. On the fourth pass the cell breaks off and drops back into the opening figure.",
   "law": "The cell is nine eighths long in a bar of eight, so each repeat slides half a beat against the drums. The ear hears the same notes but loses the downbeat; the opening figure and the landing on the open A give the downbeat back.",
